{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וככה", :translit "ukhakha", :gloss "and thus"} {:he "וככה תאכלו אותו", :translit "ukhakha tokh'lu oto", :gloss "and thus you shall eat it"} {:he "וככה יהיה נעור", :translit "ukhakha yihyeh na'or", :gloss "and thus he shall be roused"} {:he "כשהשביע לבני הגולה לעזוב המשא", :translit "kshehishbia livnei hagola la'azov hamasa", :gloss "when he adjured the members of the exile to abandon the burden"} {:he "דאתקש ביאה שניה לביאה ראשונה", :translit "datikash bi'ah shniyah levi'ah rishonah", :gloss "for the second coming is linked to the first coming"} {:he "ראוי היה ליעשות להם נס בימי עזרא כמו שנעשה בימי משה אלא שגרם החטא", :translit "ra'ui haya le'iyasot lahem nes bimei ezra kemo shena'aseh bimei moshe ella shegaram hachet", :gloss "it would have been fitting for a miracle to be done for them in the days of Ezra as was done in the days of Moses, except that sin caused"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וככה תאכלו אותו" "וככה יהיה נעור"]}], :frame {:text "The link between the exodus from Egypt and the return from Babylonian exile is established in the Talmud: the verse וככה יהיה נעור appears in Ezra's adjuration of the exiles (Ezra 10:8), and the rabbinic derashah at Sanhedrin 93b expounds that the second redemption should have mirrored the first, complete with miracles as in the days of Moses, but was diminished because of sin.", :sources ["Ezra 10:8" "Sanhedrin 93b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "חגורים", :translit "chagurim", :gloss "girded"} {:he "מתניכם חגורים", :translit "motneikhem chagurim", :gloss "your loins girded"} {:he "ושש מאות איש חגורים", :translit "veshesh me'ot ish chagurim", :gloss "and six hundred men girded"} {:he "והנה איש אחד לבוש בדים ומתניו חגורים", :translit "vehineh ish echad lavush badim umotnav chagurim", :gloss "and behold a certain man clothed in linen and his loins girded"} {:he "שפסל מיכה עבר עמהם בים", :translit "shepesel mikha avar imam bayam", :gloss "that the idol of Micah crossed with them in the sea"} {:he "ואידך", :translit "ve'idach", :gloss "and the other"} {:he "צדיקים שבהם דומים למלאכי השרת", :translit "tzadikim shebahem domim lemal'achei hasharet", :gloss "the righteous among them are like the ministering angels"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["מתניכם חגורים" "ושש מאות איש חגורים" "ומתניו חגורים"]}], :frame {:text "The tradition that the idol of Micah traveled with the tribe of Dan across the sea is found at Sanhedrin 103b. The vision of the man clothed in linen with loins girded appears in Daniel 10:5, interpreted by rabbinic tradition as the angel Gabriel (Sanhedrin 93b). The comparison of Israel's righteous to ministering angels is a rabbinic motif found in contexts such as Shabbat 25b.", :sources ["Judges 18:16" "Sanhedrin 103b" "Daniel 10:5" "Sanhedrin 93b" "Shabbat 25b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בחפזון", :translit "bechipazon", :gloss "in haste"} {:he "כי בחפזון יצאת מארץ מצרים", :translit "ki bechipazon yatzatah me'eretz mitzrayim", :gloss "for in haste you left the land of Egypt"} {:he "כי לא בחפזון תצאו", :translit "ki lo bechipazon tetze'u", :gloss "for not in haste shall you go out"} {:he "דלאו בחפזון דישראל היה", :translit "delav bechipazon deyisrael haya", :gloss "that it was not in haste of Israel"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["בחפזון" "כי בחפזון יצאת מארץ מצרים" "כי לא בחפזון תצאו"]}], :frame {:text "The rabbinic derashah on the exodus from Egypt in haste is linked to Deuteronomy 16:3, where כי בחפזון יצאת מארץ מצרים is read so that the haste is attributed to the Egyptians' pressing the Israelites out rather than the Israelites' own hurry, as stated at Berakhot 9a where the verse is understood in connection with the plague of the firstborn.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 16:3" "Berakhot 9a" "Isaiah 52:12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וככה תאכלו אותו" "וככה יהיה נעור"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וככה תאכלו אותו", :refs ["Exodus 12:11"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "וככה יהיה נעור", :refs ["Nehemiah 5:13"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["מתניכם חגורים" "ושש מאות איש חגורים" "ומתניו חגורים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "מתניכם חגורים", :refs ["Exodus 12:11"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ושש מאות איש חגורים", :refs ["Judges 18:16"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ומתניו חגורים", :refs ["Daniel 10:5"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["בחפזון" "כי בחפזון יצאת מארץ מצרים" "כי לא בחפזון תצאו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "בחפזון", :refs ["Exodus 12:11" "Deuteronomy 16:3" "Isaiah 52:12"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כי בחפזון יצאת מארץ מצרים", :refs ["Deuteronomy 16:3"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כי לא בחפזון תצאו", :refs ["Isaiah 52:12"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:15:24.469375737Z", :model "glm-5.2"}